# 🚗 AutoTrack — Car Service & Maintenance Tracker

A full-stack web application built with **Spring Boot**, **MongoDB Atlas**, and **Vanilla JS**.

---

## 🗂 Project Structure

```
autotrack/
├── autotrack-backend/    ← Spring Boot REST API
└── autotrack-frontend/   ← HTML/CSS/JS Frontend
```

---

## ⚙️ Backend Setup (Spring Boot)

### 1. Prerequisites
- Java 17+
- Maven 3.8+
- MongoDB Atlas account

### 2. Configure MongoDB Atlas
Edit `autotrack-backend/src/main/resources/application.properties`:
```properties
spring.data.mongodb.uri=mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@<cluster>.mongodb.net/autotrack?retryWrites=true&w=majority
```

### 3. Configure Email (Gmail)
```properties
spring.mail.username=your-email@gmail.com
spring.mail.password=your-16-char-app-password
```
> ⚠️ Use a Gmail **App Password** (not your regular password).  
> Enable 2FA → Google Account → Security → App Passwords.

### 4. Run the Backend
```bash
cd autotrack-backend
mvn spring-boot:run
```
Backend starts on **http://localhost:8080**

---

## 🌐 Frontend Setup

### Option A — Live Server (VS Code)
1. Install **Live Server** extension in VS Code
2. Open `autotrack-frontend/index.html`
3. Click **Go Live** in the status bar
4. Frontend runs on `http://127.0.0.1:5500`

### Option B — Python HTTP Server
```bash
cd autotrack-frontend
python3 -m http.server 5500
```
Open `http://localhost:5500`

